  ('LPS-ARC-008', NULL, 'Armenian Catholics are one of the six Eastern Catholic communities sharing the unified 1949 Personal Status Law. They recognize the authority of the Pope while maintaining Armenian liturgical and cultural traditions. The 1990 Code of Canons of Eastern Churches (CCEO) introduced spousal equality provisions (Canon 777) that apply to all Eastern Catholic churches. The Armenian Catholic Church has its own patriarchate and follows the Code of Procedure for Tribunals of Eastern Catholic Churches for court procedures.', 'en', 'Personal Status Law of the Armenian Catholic Confession — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Personal Status - Armenian Catholic'),
  ('LPS-SYO-009', 'General', 'Réglementation des affaires de mariage, divorce, garde et héritage', 'fr', 'Personal Status Law of the Syriac Orthodox Confession, Article General', 'General provisions', 'Personal Status - Syriac Orthodox'),
  ('LPS-SYO-009', 'General', 'تنظيم شؤون الزواج والطلاق والحضانة والميراث', 'ar', 'Personal Status Law of the Syriac Orthodox Confession, Article General', 'General provisions', 'Personal Status - Syriac Orthodox'),
  ('LPS-SYO-009', NULL, 'The Syriac Orthodox Church is one of the ancient Oriental Orthodox churches. Their personal status law was renewed in 2003 by the Synod of Antioch and ratified by Patriarch Ignatius Zakka I.', 'en', 'Personal Status Law of the Syriac Orthodox Confession — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Personal Status - Syriac Orthodox'),
