  ('LPS-SYC-010', 'Article 865 (CCEO)', 'السلطة الأبوية من حق الأب، مع مراعاة مصلحة الطفل الفضلى', 'ar', 'Personal Status Law of the Syriac Catholic Confession, Article Article 865 (CCEO)', 'Parental authority and child''s best interest', 'Personal Status - Syriac Catholic'),
  ('LPS-SYC-010', NULL, 'Syriac Catholics are one of the six Eastern Catholic communities sharing the unified 1949 Personal Status Law. They recognize the authority of the Pope while maintaining West Syriac liturgical traditions. The 1990 Code of Canons of Eastern Churches (CCEO) introduced significant reforms including spousal equality (Canon 777). The Syriac Catholic Church has its own patriarchate (the Syriac Catholic Patriarchate of Antioch) and follows the Code of Procedure for Tribunals of Eastern Catholic Churches. The community has ancient roots in the Levant and maintains distinct cultural and religious traditions.', 'en', 'Personal Status Law of the Syriac Catholic Confession — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Personal Status - Syriac Catholic'),
