  ('LPS-CHL-011', 'Article 865 (CCEO)', 'Autorité parentale au père, considérant intérêt supérieur de l''enfant', 'fr', 'Personal Status Law of the Chaldean Catholic Confession, Article Article 865 (CCEO)', 'Parental authority', 'Personal Status - Chaldean Catholic'),
  ('LPS-CHL-011', 'Article 865 (CCEO)', 'السلطة الأبوية من حق الأب، مع مراعاة مصلحة الطفل الفضلى', 'ar', 'Personal Status Law of the Chaldean Catholic Confession, Article Article 865 (CCEO)', 'Parental authority', 'Personal Status - Chaldean Catholic'),
  ('LPS-CHL-011', NULL, 'Chaldean Catholics are one of the six Eastern Catholic communities sharing the unified 1949 Personal Status Law. They recognize the authority of the Pope while maintaining East Syriac liturgical traditions. The 1990 Code of Canons of Eastern Churches (CCEO) introduced significant reforms including spousal equality (Canon 777). The Chaldean Catholic Church has its own patriarchate (the Chaldean Catholic Patriarchate of Babylon) based in Baghdad, with diaspora communities throughout the world including Lebanon. Many Chaldeans in Lebanon are refugees from Iraq. The community follows the Code of Procedure for Tribunals of Eastern Catholic Churches.', 'en', 'Personal Status Law of the Chaldean Catholic Confession — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Personal Status - Chaldean Catholic'),
